WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.126
Surtsey is already disappearing.

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:08.079
Surtsey has two tuff cones, a lava shield in the south,

00:00:08.079 --> 00:00:12.305
and a low spit of eroded sand and gravel on its sheltered northern side.

00:00:12.305 --> 00:00:16.355
North Atlantic storms have cut high cliffs into its south-west coast.

00:00:17.455 --> 00:00:20.026
By 2012 the island had lost half its area.

00:00:20.026 --> 00:00:23.208
The loose material and lava apron will keep eroding,

00:00:23.208 --> 00:00:26.023
but the hard tuff cores will last much longer,

00:00:26.023 --> 00:00:29.205
as small steep stacks like the older Westman islets.

00:00:30.305 --> 00:00:35.653
Surtsey shows in decades what the General Dynamic Model describes over millions of years:

00:00:35.653 --> 00:00:38.838
an island's area and height peak early, then decline.
